### E1/E2 red

Added [test_fixtures_test.exs](/home/jes/sol-e2c-tmp1/wt/test/co
mmonplace_next/test_fixtures_test.exs:1).

Before the fix:

```text
Running ExUnit with seed: 0

1) fixture roots do not collide across fresh VMs
   Refute with == failed, both sides are exactly equal
   left: "/tmp/commonplace-next-collision-arm-1"

2) cleanup waits for a captured child pid before removing its ro
ot
   cleanup returned while child pid 1576 was still alive

2 tests, 2 failures
```

E1 deterministically showed two fresh VMs selecting the same roo
t while the stale marker remained.

E2 showed `File.rm_rf!/1` returning while the planted slow child
 was still alive. I did not reproduce an actual `File.rm_rf!/1`
exception in the plant, so I do not claim that part of E2 red.

A full-suite diagnostic later reproduced the underlying race mor
e directly: a current pid-prefixed `e2c` root was deleted and th
en recreated by a child whose wrapper had already died. That led
 to retaining the pid in the outer fixture context and waiting u
nconditionally.

### E1/E2 green

```text
Running ExUnit with seed: 0

..
Finished in 2.0 seconds
2 tests, 0 failures
```

The stale E1 root remains untouched, the new VM selects another
root, and E2 removal occurs only after the planted child pid is
gone.

Relevant integration validation:

```text
remote_editor + loopback_gateway + two_organization:
41 tests, 0 failures

remote_editor + two_organization after unconditional-pid fix:
30 tests, 0 failures

gateway_listener_lifetime:
4 tests, 0 failures
directory count: 2948 -> 2948
```

### Full-suite controls

The repository-local `tmp/test-data` was cleared before the suit
e using `File.rm_rf!/1` because the sandbox rejected the request
ed literal `rm -rf`. No host `/tmp` entry was deleted.

There were 2,950 pre-existing `commonplace-next-*` directories b
y the final controls:

```text
Control 1, seed 104729: 2950 before -> 2950 after
Control 2, seed 130363: 2950 before -> 2950 after
```

Thus both runs left zero new matching directories.

The normal second full run result was:

```text
513 tests, 5 failures, 1 excluded
```

All five failures were environmental repository gates:

- four private-origin pin checks could not authenticate to GitHu
b;
- the trust-root falsifier could not restore `config/dev.exs` be
cause `.git` is read-only.

The falsifier’s added config stanza was manually restored afterw
ard. No task-related functional test failed.

Final checks:

```text
mix format --check-formatted: PASS
git diff --check: PASS
E1/E2 targeted tests: 2 tests, 0 failures
lib/ changes: none
