Implemented the fixture-root and child-cleanup fixes. No files u
nder `lib/` changed.

### Provisioning limitation

The workspace was already clean at the required commit:

```text
ee7fb9400df93c8c369b39afeab9750c0a6c124f
origin = git@github.com:commonplace-systems/commonplace-next.git
origin/main = ee7fb9400df93c8c369b39afeab9750c0a6c124f
```

However, the mandated remote verification and branch creation co
uld not be completed:

```text
git ls-remote ...:
git@github.com: Permission denied (publickey).

git switch -c sol/next-e2c-tmp-1 ...:
.git/index.lock: Read-only file system
```

The environment has no SSH agent/key, GitHub CLI login, or HTTPS
 credential, and `.git` is mounted read-only. Changes therefore
remain in the worktree on `main`, not on `sol/next-e2c-tmp-1`.

### Implementation

Added [test_fixtures.ex](/home/jes/sol-e2c-tmp1/wt/test/support/
test_fixtures.ex:1), defining `CommonplaceNext.TestFixtures.uniq
ue_tmp_root/1,2`. It follows the existing precedent exactly:

```elixir
unique = "#{:os.getpid()}-#{System.unique_integer([:positive, :m
onotonic])}"
```

The human-readable tag remains in every path.

Enhanced [second_beam.ex](/home/jes/sol-e2c-tmp1/wt/test/support
/second_beam.ex:66):

- `wait_gone!/2` polls the captured OS pid with a bounded timeou
t.
- Timeout raises loudly with the pid.
- `reap/1` now waits after KILL rather than returning immediatel
y.

`remote_editor`, `loopback_gateway`, and `two_organization` now
retain the child OS pid outside the GenServer wrapper and wait u
nconditionally before deleting the fixture root—even if the wrap
per has already died.

The listener-lifetime fixtures also now move the application awa
y from their store paths and remove both fixture directories wit
h `File.rm_rf!/1`.

